cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or build on these results, please cite it as below."
title: "zero-shot-bci: cross-session EEG-BCI personalization research code"
abstract: >-
  Research code, results, and a negative-results log for closing the
  calibration-to-live-session accuracy gap in motor-imagery brain-computer
  interfaces. Evaluated on BCI Competition IV-2a/2b with OpenBMI and PhysioNet
  as external population pools. The best cross-session result is CSP+LDA with
  per-session Riemannian alignment (66.9%, 4-class, 9 subjects, chance 25%);
  every method that directly compares two different subjects' covariance
  structure is documented as null or harmful.
authors:
  - family-names: Marinov
    given-names: Hristo
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-10-07
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/hrmarinov/zero-shot-bci"
type: software
keywords:
  - EEG
  - brain-computer interface
  - motor imagery
  - cross-session adaptation
  - transfer learning
  - Riemannian geometry
  - BCI illiteracy
